    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0675" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Italy/289: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-06-05T17:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1936—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. Your 185, June 1, 5 p.m. The notification sent to the Italian Ambassador May
                    22, 1936,<anchor n="50" xml:id="d485-f1"/> states that this Government is fully
                    disposed to discuss, through diplomatic channels, any proposals which the
                    Italian Government may desire to put forward in regard to the payment of its
                    indebtedness to the United States, and that such proposals would receive careful
                    consideration with a view to eventual submission to the American Congress.</p>
                <pb facs="0676" n="596" xml:id="pg596"/>
                <p>The Department would be glad to discuss informally any proposals that the Italian
                    Government may initiate through diplomatic channels at Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
